{"seq":13,"slug":"environmental-anthropology","title":"环境人类学","stage":"DONE","category":"anthropology","chapterCount":4,"docCount":12,"url":"/h/anthropology/environmental-anthropology","rating":{"composite":3.66,"verdict":"stable","groups":{"quality":3.6,"coverage":3.5,"positioning":3.5,"strategic":4},"weights":{"quality":0.3,"coverage":0.25,"positioning":0.2,"strategic":0.25},"profile":null},"introMarkdown":"# 环境人类学\n\n人类从来不是悬浮在真空里的物种。我们呼吸的空气、脚下的土壤、餐桌上的食物、头顶上的电网，无一不把「文化」与「自然」缠绕成一团难解的线。环境人类学就是专门去拆解这团线的学科——它追问人群如何理解、利用、改造他们栖居的环境，又如何被环境反过来塑造。它不满足于把环境当作背景板，而是把人与非人、社会与生态之间的相互构成，本身当作研究对象。\n\n这个 hub 由四条主线层层递进地组织起来，从理论根基一直推到当下最锋利的前沿争论。\n\n第一条主线是「理论基础」。它交代环境人类学如何从博厄斯学派对环境决定论的反叛中走出，经由斯图尔德的文化生态学把生计技术与环境的关系系统化，再经由拉帕波特等人把生态系统与能量流引入民族志，最后在二十世纪七八十年代被政治生态学彻底改写——人们意识到森林退化、土壤侵蚀往往不是「无知农民」的错，而是权力、资本与殖民历史的产物。这条线确立了本学科最核心的张力：环境问题到底是技术适应问题，还是政治经济问题。\n\n第二条主线是「知识与实践」。如果说理论基础回答「研究者怎么看」，这条线则回答「当地人怎么看」。传统生态知识、民族生物学的本土分类、以及把动物与其它物种重新拉回民族志中心的多物种研究，共同构成了对「只有科学才算知识」这一傲慢的有力反驳。\n\n第三条主线是「当代危机」。气候变化、灾害、资源争夺，这些不再是遥远的理论命题，而是正在重塑无数社区命运的现实。人类学在这里的贡献，是揭示同一场风暴、同一片矿区，为何对不同人群意味着截然不同的风险与不公。\n\n第四条主线是「前沿议题」。人类世概念与本体论转向逼着学科重新追问「自然」到底是什么；保护实践中的暴力与原住民权利的角力仍在继续；而能源与基础设施人类学则把电缆、管道、数据中心这些「看不见的庞然大物」推到台前。\n\n四条线不是并列的抽屉，而是一条不断深化的螺旋：从理论，到本土知识，到危机现实，再到对学科根基本身的反思。读完整个 hub，你应当能用人类学的眼光，重新看待任何一处「人与环境」的现场。\n","chapters":[{"seq":1,"slug":"theory-foundations","title":"理论基础","docCount":3,"url":"/h/anthropology/environmental-anthropology/theory-foundations","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"intro-and-lineage","title":"环境人类学导论与谱系","url":"/h/anthropology/environmental-anthropology/theory-foundations/intro-and-lineage"},{"seq":2,"slug":"cultural-ecology","title":"文化生态学与生态人类学","url":"/h/anthropology/environmental-anthropology/theory-foundations/cultural-ecology"},{"seq":3,"slug":"political-ecology","title":"政治生态学","url":"/h/anthropology/environmental-anthropology/theory-foundations/political-ecology"}]},{"seq":2,"slug":"knowledge-practice","title":"知识与实践","docCount":3,"url":"/h/anthropology/environmental-anthropology/knowledge-practice","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"traditional-ecological-knowledge","title":"传统生态知识（TEK）","url":"/h/anthropology/environmental-anthropology/knowledge-practice/traditional-ecological-knowledge"},{"seq":2,"slug":"ethnobiology-folk-classification","title":"民族生物学与本土分类","url":"/h/anthropology/environmental-anthropology/knowledge-practice/ethnobiology-folk-classification"},{"seq":3,"slug":"multispecies-ethnography","title":"人与动物与多物种民族志","url":"/h/anthropology/environmental-anthropology/knowledge-practice/multispecies-ethnography"}]},{"seq":3,"slug":"contemporary-crises","title":"当代危机","docCount":3,"url":"/h/anthropology/environmental-anthropology/contemporary-crises","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"anthropology-of-climate-change","title":"气候变化的人类学","url":"/h/anthropology/environmental-anthropology/contemporary-crises/anthropology-of-climate-change"},{"seq":2,"slug":"disaster-vulnerability","title":"灾害与脆弱性","url":"/h/anthropology/environmental-anthropology/contemporary-crises/disaster-vulnerability"},{"seq":3,"slug":"resource-conflict-environmental-justice","title":"资源冲突与环境正义","url":"/h/anthropology/environmental-anthropology/contemporary-crises/resource-conflict-environmental-justice"}]},{"seq":4,"slug":"frontiers","title":"前沿议题","docCount":3,"url":"/h/anthropology/environmental-anthropology/frontiers","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"anthropocene-ontological-turn","title":"人类世与本体论转向","url":"/h/anthropology/environmental-anthropology/frontiers/anthropocene-ontological-turn"},{"seq":2,"slug":"conservation-and-indigenous","title":"保护与原住民","url":"/h/anthropology/environmental-anthropology/frontiers/conservation-and-indigenous"},{"seq":3,"slug":"energy-infrastructure-anthropology","title":"能源与基础设施人类学","url":"/h/anthropology/environmental-anthropology/frontiers/energy-infrastructure-anthropology"}]}]}